# Standalone clone of the MCP server (chungweeeei/SyncAI-ROS-MCP), if anyone keeps
# one here as a local scratch copy. It is a different repository's working tree and
# must never be committed into this one; the vendored in-tree copy it used to
# shadow (src/syncai_ros_mcp) was removed, and lives in git history now.
src/syncai-ros-mcp/

# LIO map output (pcd / gridmap / poses — regenerated, not tracked).
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `map/` matches a directory of that name at
# any depth, and it was silently swallowing
# src/syncai_backend/syncai_backend/repositories/map/. Files already tracked there
# stayed visible, so nothing looked wrong until a new module in it went missing
# from a commit.
/map/

# TTS model weights (kokoro-onnx: kokoro-v1.0.onnx + voices-v1.0.bin, ~330 MB —
# downloaded once from the kokoro-onnx GitHub releases, see
# src/syncai_backend/gateways/tts/tts.py for the exact URLs). Anchored for the
# same reason as /map/ above: a bare `models/` would swallow any future
# src/**/models/ package directory.
/models/

# Hand- and API-recorded rosbags (record/<name>/*.db3 + metadata.yaml, written
# by POST /api/v1/recordings or by `ros2 bag record` in a shell). Anchored with
# a leading slash for the reason /map/ and /models/ above give: a bare
# `record/` matches a directory of that name at any depth, and would silently
# swallow a future src/**/record/ package directory.
/record/

# Materialised by `vcs import < interface.repos`, not committed -- the same
# arrangement src/third-party/ has. It was 28 tracked files in this repo until
# the 2026-09 split moved it to SyncAI-Robot-Interface, so that syncai_backend
# could build against the interfaces without checking out the whole workspace.
# Edit the messages THERE; a change made in this directory is untracked and the
# next --force import overwrites it.
src/syncai_common/

# Materialised by `vcs import < backend.repos`, not committed. Tracked here as
# 120 files until the 2026-09 split; the copy had diverged from
# SyncAI-Robot-Backend across 44 files, which is the divergence this ends.
# Edit the code THERE; a change made in this directory is untracked and the
# next --force import overwrites it.
src/syncai_backend/
